<title>MONACO: RALLYING-LEADING MONTE CARLO PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>RALLYING-LEADING MONTE CARLO PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>MONTE CARLO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading overall placings in</p>
<p>the Monte Carlo world championship rally after three timed</p>
<p>stages on Monday:</p>
<p> 1. Carlos Sainz (Spain) Ford Escort	  33 minutes 15</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p> 2. Tommi Makinen (Finland) Mitsubishi Lancer	 33:19</p>
<p> 3. Colin McRae (Britain) Subaru Impreza		33:38</p>
<p> 4. Piero Liatti (Italy) Subaru Impreza		 33:49</p>
<p> 5. Didier Auriol (France) Ford Escort		  33:56</p>
<p> 6. Armin Schwarz (Germany) Ford Escort		 34:19</p>
<p> 7. Dieter Depping (Germany) Ford Escort		34:24</p>
<p> 8. Freddy Loix (Belgium) Toyota Celica		 34:56</p>
<p> 9. Uwe Nittel (Germany) Mitsubishi Lancer	    35:11</p>
<p> 10. Henrik Lundgaard (Denmark) Toyota Celica	 35:34</p>
